title: "Microtubule-Stars: classical Kuramoto ring with holographic phase-pattern recall under a slow model drive (SYNTHETIC)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/microtubule-stars"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC. Standard-library Python classical Kuramoto simulation: a ring
  of phase oscillators stores phase-patterns as one interference record and
  recalls by projection. An optional slow multi-mode oscillation
  (stellar-pulsation-style model, not stellar data) modulates coupling gain.
  Measured: unstructured modulation degrades recall monotonically, with no
  1:1 phase locking across scales. No quantum mechanics and no consciousness
  model are simulated; no claim of cosmic influence on brains.
keywords:
